Package: lockd
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3-yaml,
 polkitd | policykit-1,
 pkexec,
 bash (>= 5.0),
Recommends: ufw, fail2ban
Suggests: clamav, clamav-daemon, clamav-freshclam
Description: Modular Linux security hardening tool (core + CLI)
 Lockd applies, simulates and verifies security hardening on Linux
 systems through declarative, reversible modules. Every change can be
 previewed with a real dry-run and rolled back afterwards; the reported
 state comes from the real system, not from a cached file.
 .
 This package contains the core engine, the command-line interface, the
 interactive TUI, the hardening modules and the privileged Polkit helper.
 Install lockd-gtk for the graphical interface.

